<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:50:51 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Business</category><title>France intends to borrow record €340 billion as Covid-era debt comes due</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/business/20260929-france-intends-to-borrow-record-340-billion-euros-covid-era-debt-comes-due</link><description>
The French ​government will sell a record amount of bonds to investors next year as it faces a surge in Covid-era debt due for redemption and needing to be refinanced, the public debt management ​office ‌said on Tuesday amid mounting concern about France's surging public deficit and borrowing rates. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcca8ba8-bc44-11f1-8cd1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UZ6L2-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcca8ba8-bc44-11f1-8cd1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UZ6L2-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d573df34-bc43-11f1-88bb-9325e8e3e35e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:34:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcca8ba8-bc44-11f1-8cd1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UZ6L2-1.jpg">© Thomas Samson, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Ugandan coronation under social media scrutiny</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-coronation-under-social-media-scrutiny</link><description>
In tonight's edition, Uganda's new king of Tooro is crowned before thousands. Also, Africa's richest man cautions the continent against losing control of its major projects. And dozens of civilians are killed as Ethiopian government forces bombard towns in the northern region of Tigray.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcb65eb4-bc42-11f1-aaec-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260929-2140-Live-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcb65eb4-bc42-11f1-aaec-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260929-2140-Live-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42eb5b4c-bc43-11f1-8780-1503ea2b1e62</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:22:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>One in eight cancers worldwide linked to infections, WHO agency says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/one-in-eight-cancers-worldwide-linked-to-infections-who-agency-says</link><description>
A new study from the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) shows that an estimated 2.3 million new cancer cases worldwide in 2024 – about 12% of all new cancer cases – were caused by infections and could be prevented with treatment or vaccines. FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin speaks with the lead author of the study, Dr Gary Clifford, Scientist at the IARC.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecfd7f4a-bc3c-11f1-b6e1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-210545-211620-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecfd7f4a-bc3c-11f1-b6e1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-210545-211620-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f251cd7a-bc3c-11f1-8add-fbab6e8c354d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:03:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Mystery over UK airbase scare as police find 'quantity of petrol' but no explosives</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives</link><description>
Britain's counter-terrorism police said ​on Tuesday that no improvised explosive devices had been found as part of an ​investigation ‌into a suspected plot targeting ⁠a British airbase used by US forces to ‌strike Iran, deepening uncertainty over the incident a day after five UK-based suspects were released on bail. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f6d90c6-bc36-11f1-97c7-c77776d3fb00</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:05:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg">© Alastair Grant, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Burnham sets out 'new path' for Britain, vows to seek consensus on ties with EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu</link><description>
UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham pledged Tuesday to give Britain "a new social contract for the 21st century", reform the country's electoral system and build consensus on a new relationship with the European Union as he set out a long-term vision to tackle the UK's woes in his first speech as leader at the annual Labour party conference.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">240bcb0e-bc29-11f1-a4cb-f7d59cc60f65</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:54:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg">© Temilade Adelaja, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Marrakesh mayor Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri becomes first woman prime minister of Morocco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">08ad3d38-bc20-11f1-8b55-97484190506c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:09:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Morocco's king appoints Marrakesh mayor El Mansouri as first woman prime minister</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote</link><description>
King Mohammed VI appointed Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri as Morocco's first woman prime minister on Tuesday after her liberal-centrist party came out on top in a September 23 parliamentary election, the royal palace said. Her government is expected to make major investments linked to the 2030 FIFA World Cup, while facing pressing issues including unemployment and living costs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c40d9ce-b80a-11f1-a259-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259696087967.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c40d9ce-b80a-11f1-a259-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259696087967.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">754081dc-bc1e-11f1-80d8-a15541d9f1cb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:08:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c40d9ce-b80a-11f1-a259-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259696087967.jpg">© Mosa'ab Elshamy, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Legion of Honour: Police investigate corruption claims for France’s top award</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-legion-of-honour-police-investigate-corruption-claims-for-france-s-top-award</link><description>
French police took a top general into custody last week as part of an ongoing probe into potential bribery among the selection committee for the country’s highest decoration, the Legion of Honour. Investigations centre on possible payoffs for awards including expansive meals, holidays and thousands of euros in cash.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202038aa-bc0f-11f1-a14f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17181434246649.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202038aa-bc0f-11f1-a14f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17181434246649.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf7e5750-bc0f-11f1-9d67-9d40f7c16032</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:43:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202038aa-bc0f-11f1-a14f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17181434246649.jpg">© Francois Mori, AP</source><dc:creator>Joanna YORK</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A view from Brazil: The fight for the favela vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-a-view-from-brazil-the-fight-for-the-favela-vote</link><description>
In Brazil, more than 158 million voters are being called to the polls on Sunday to elect their next president, as well as new members of Congress and governors. In Rio de Janeiro, local candidates are fighting for one particularly sought-after electorate: the residents of favelas. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Rocinha, Brazil’s largest favela.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7765ef70-bc13-11f1-83ae-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-162010-162541-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7765ef70-bc13-11f1-83ae-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-162010-162541-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c91657e-bc13-11f1-8ba1-4dff581b9752</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:41:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French civil servants strike, demand additional budgetary resources</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-civil-servants-strike-demand-additional-budgetary-resources</link><description>
French civil servants were mobilising in large numbers on Tuesday, with more than 170 rallies planned across France. A coalition of unions are demanding additional budgetary resources for schools, hospitals, and other public services. Among those on strike are firefighters, pushed to their limits by the summer's historic wildfires. Here's a look at one of the protests in Lyon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddb4c82-bc12-11f1-842b-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-161310-161458-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddb4c82-bc12-11f1-842b-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-161310-161458-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52871900-bc12-11f1-bdba-e31f9b37c51d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:40:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Over 100 settlers attack Occupied West Bank village, clash with Israeli forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-over-100-settlers-attack-occupied-west-bank-village-clash-with-israeli-forces</link><description>
More than 100 Israeli settlers attacked a village in the north of the occupied West Bank early Tuesday, wounding three members of Israel's security forces and burning two Palestinian homes, authorities and residents said. The attack occurred while the military was attempting to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home in the village of Jalud after they had been displaced by settler attacks two months earlier. ABC Journalist Jordana Miller reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dab256aa-bc12-11f1-be86-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-161527-161934-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dab256aa-bc12-11f1-be86-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-161527-161934-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e00352ee-bc12-11f1-a97e-d12129d31be6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:38:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eiffel Tower chief to step down over removal of women staff during Hindu group's visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-eiffel-tower-chief-to-step-down-over-removal-of-women-staff-during-hindu-group-visit-baps</link><description>
The head of the Eiffel Tower is set to step down in the wake of a controversy sparked by the removal of female workers during a private visit of the Paris landmark by members of the Hindu sect BAPS, which triggered a staff walkout earlier this month and sparked outrage in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1164fca6-abc0-11f1-a24c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1164fca6-abc0-11f1-a24c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b85f821e-bc10-11f1-89fe-7b0f1abdd3bc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:22:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1164fca6-abc0-11f1-a24c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE-1.jpg">© Kenzo Tribouillard, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French far-right leader Bardella denies anti-Semitism accusations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-far-right-leader-bardella-denies-anti-semitism-accusations</link><description>
🇫🇷 ✡️ Far-right #NationalRally (RN) party leader Jordan #Bardella has denied accusation by French investigative website #Mediapart that he made anti-Semitic comments on private chats in 2013. It comes as RN candidate Marine #LePen is polling well in the lead for the 2027 presidential election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7947fb80-bc0e-11f1-a74a-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/Bardella-Thumb-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7947fb80-bc0e-11f1-a74a-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/Bardella-Thumb-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9fafa8cc-bc0e-11f1-936f-f507e29d49f5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:11:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's Le Pen defiant after top ally hit by antisemitism claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-france-s-le-pen-defiant-after-top-ally-hit-by-antisemitism-claims</link><description>
French far-right presidential candidate Marine Le Pen on Tuesday vowed to hit back at allegations of antisemitism targeting her de-facto number two Jordan Bardella, which have punctured her buoyant campaign at a time she is riding high in the polls. Le Pen, who is aiming to win the Elysee at her fourth attempt next year in a far-right breakthrough that would send a shockwave across Europe, lambasted the Mediapart website that published the claims and said Bardella has her "total confidence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00bb515e-bc0d-11f1-a3c1-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-150200-150409-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00bb515e-bc0d-11f1-a3c1-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-150200-150409-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">05ebd130-bc0d-11f1-b2cd-1b0591d395d1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:10:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Calais Jungle: A child and 2 women killed during Channel crossing attempt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-calais-jungle-a-child-and-2-women-killed-during-channel-crossing-attempt</link><description>
A 10-year-old child and two women died Monday on the treacherous migration route across the English Channel from France, apparently trampled to death on a boat packed with more than 100 people, French authorities said. The so-called “taxi boat" ran into difficulty off the northern French coast, with its passengers asking for help, authorities said. Such inflatable boats attempt the dangerous crossing after picking up people from the beaches of northern France, where they wade into the sea to clamber aboard. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451c5d88-bc0e-11f1-bb6e-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-151754-152651-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451c5d88-bc0e-11f1-bb6e-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-151754-152651-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a762fe8-bc0e-11f1-8c87-cda89ee41657</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:09:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish royals welcome French President Macron in official ceremony</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-spanish-royals-welcome-french-president-macron-in-official-ceremony</link><description>
Spain's King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia welcomed French President Emmanuel Macron and his wife Brigitte Macron during an official ceremony upon their arrival at Madrid's Royal Palace. French President Macron is on a two-day official visit in Spain. This state visit will serve to highlight and strengthen the ties and bilateral relations between the two countries. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0196d066-bc0e-11f1-ac9b-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-152718-152850-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0196d066-bc0e-11f1-ac9b-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-152718-152850-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06ce4a1e-bc0e-11f1-a6cc-4d93b0657460</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:08:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>OpenAI cancels release of newest model due to safety concerns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-openai-cancels-release-of-newest-model-due-to-safety-concerns</link><description>
OpenAI will not release its newest artificial intelligence model, known as Astra 6.1, after internal testing by the ChatGPT-maker revealed it did not meet safety standards, the company confirmed Monday. Concerns about AI safety have escalated in recent months after models developed by OpenAI and rival lab Anthropic were involved in security incidents during testing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ede5670c-bc0e-11f1-bd99-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17233986026abbc5d4df8312-21000185.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ede5670c-bc0e-11f1-bd99-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17233986026abbc5d4df8312-21000185.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a31cd9f8-bc0e-11f1-aa3a-a9eac7c72494</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Can Parisians really teach us to be happier?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260929-can-parisians-really-teach-us-to-be-happier</link><description>
We welcome back Alex Durand and Tom Carles – better known as AT Frenchies – to talk France, America, friendship and the pursuit of happiness. The childhood friends-turned-internet phenomenon are back with their new book, "Pardon Our French". From growing up together to building a life between France and the US, Alex and Tom share their unique take on what makes Parisians tick, their transatlantic journey, their love of two cultures and the challenges of writing a book together.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3eeda76a-bc03-11f1-91b1-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AT-FRENCHIES-29-09-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3eeda76a-bc03-11f1-91b1-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AT-FRENCHIES-29-09-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b7e9e10-bc04-11f1-bb91-23c9e0ad7af4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:22:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Amanda ALEXANDER</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Interpol reflect on dystopian times on new album 'This Mirror Weighs a Ton'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260929-interpol-reflect-on-dystopian-times-on-new-album-this-mirror-weighs-a-ton</link><description>
In this edition of arts24, Jennifer Ben Brahim meets founding member and lead guitarist of Interpol, Daniel Kessler. They are one of New York's defining bands, keeping the spirit of indie sleaze alive for nearly three decades. The post-punk rockers first drew attention with "Turn on the Bright Lights", laying the foundations for their icy, atmospheric sound and instantly recognisable guitar lines. They're back with their eighth album, "This Mirror Weighs a Ton", a reflection on the troubling times we're living through, from surveillance to the rise of AI.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5325b4e-bbfd-11f1-84c9-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18714651196abba940ca09f3-12215228.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5325b4e-bbfd-11f1-84c9-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18714651196abba940ca09f3-12215228.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec07cc00-bbfe-11f1-8ccb-e9d2847f2565</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:00:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Putin's goal is to prolong his power in Russia': Journalist Roman Badanin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin</link><description>
A journalist who has spent more than 20 years investigating Russian leader Vladimir Putin and who is recognised as perhaps Russia's finest investigative journalist has told FRANCE 24 that Putin's aim with the war in Ukraine is simply to prolong his power inside Russia. Roman Badanin has just published a book, "Le Tsar en personne" or "The Tsar in person" which delves into exactly how Putin's mind works. Badanin says Putin acts like a gang member, and his attitude is that "if you beat me, I will beat you even harder". The book is so far out in Russian and French, with an English version to follow. He spoke to us in Perspective.
