French presidential frontrunner Marine Le Pen on Tuesday denounced an attempt to "derail" her Élysée Palace run after a media report accused the head of her far-right National Rally (RN) party, Jordan Bardella, of making ant-Semitic comments in 2013. Le Pen said Bardella, who is tipped to be prime minister if she wins the presidency, had her "total confidence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a9f2142-bc02-11f1-802a-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/191c2d6c2fa59b9137ed69f72204c81d237ccfd9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a9f2142-bc02-11f1-802a-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/191c2d6c2fa59b9137ed69f72204c81d237ccfd9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b97a704-bc02-11f1-8bbb-ad34ceb9e2f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:33:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a9f2142-bc02-11f1-802a-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/191c2d6c2fa59b9137ed69f72204c81d237ccfd9.jpg">© Anne-Christine Poujoulat, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu's secret trip to UAE amid report of Abu Dhabi warning of Oct. 7 attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-netanyahu-s-secret-trip-to-uae-amid-report-of-abu-dhabi-warning-of-oct-7-attack</link><description>
The Israeli prime minister held an hourlong meeting with the UAE’s president on Sunday, according to two people briefed on Netanyahu's trip, which was first reported by Israel’s Channel 12 TV station. One of them said the talks focused on a report published by the Israeli daily Haaretz earlier this month that said the Emirati leader warned Netanyahu about a looming attack by Hamas just ahead of Oct. 7, 2023. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/171b3fae-bbf9-11f1-afdf-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-131440-132031-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/171b3fae-bbf9-11f1-afdf-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-131440-132031-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1caf697c-bbf9-11f1-8e09-2b7f7006bf5e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:39:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French far-right leader Bardella says filed lawsuit over anti-Semitic remarks claim</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-far-right-leader-bardella-says-filed-lawsuit-over-anti-semitic-remarks-claim</link><description>
French far-right leader Jordan Bardella said on Monday he had filed a defamation lawsuit against investigative website Mediapart over a report alleging he ​made antisemitic remarks ‌in private messages over a decade ago, saying the story was an effort to "destabilise" campaigning ahead ⁠of next year's election. The 31-year-old leads the far-right National Rally party which is seeking to clear its racist image. The party's candidate, ‌Marine Le Pen, is leading polls for the April presidential election. FRANCE 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports.
